Falsifies `pci::verification::the_msix_walk_terminates_and_bounds_its_table_size`.

The defect: the table-size field is read one bit too wide, `control & 0xfff` in place of
`control & 0x7ff`. Message Control holds the count minus one in bits 10:0, and bit 11 is
reserved; a mask written from a half-remembered "twelve bits" reads that reserved bit as part
of the count. The comment directly above the line explains the minus one and says nothing about
the width, so the slip survives a reading of its own documentation.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(cap.table_size >= 1 && cap.table_size <= 2048)`, on
any device answering with bit 11 set, where the kernel would size a vector table at up to 4096
entries against hardware that has at most 2048.

diff --git a/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs b/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/pci_configuration_space/src/lib.rs
@@ -627,3 +627,3 @@ pub fn msix_cap(bdf: Bdf, read32: &mut dyn FnMut(Bdf, u64) -> u32) -> Option<Msi
                 // has one, which is the shape of failure that looks like "no MSI-X here".
-                table_size: (control & 0x7ff) + 1,
+                table_size: (control & 0xfff) + 1,
                 table_bar: (table & 0x7) as u8,
